      "hints": [
        "Substitute the completed square form into $(4x - 3)^2 + 1 = k$.",
        "For exactly one root, set $(4x - 3)^2 = 0$ to find $k$ and the corresponding root $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set the completed square equal to $k$:\n$$(4x - 3)^2 + 1 = k \\implies (4x - 3)^2 = k - 1$$",
        "For the equation to have exactly one repeated real root, the squared term must equal zero:\n$$k - 1 = 0 \\implies k = 1$$",
        "Solve for the root $x$:\n$$4x - 3 = 0 \\implies 4x = 3 \\implies x = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$$"
      ],
